From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 15:32:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3588: point the RGA cores at the
 multicore driver

The SoC has three RGA cores -- two RGA3 and one RGA2 -- and the dtsi
describes each of them for the in-tree V4L2 rockchip-rga driver, which
binds one core per video node. Retarget all three at the vendor
multicore driver added by "video: rockchip: add multicore RGA vendor
driver", whose single /dev/rga ABI schedules work across the cores and
is what librga speaks.

Two properties per node change. The compatible selects the driver and,
for the RGA3 pair, tells the two otherwise-identical cores apart: the
vendor driver derives its per-core register layout from
rockchip,rga3_core0 / rockchip,rga3_core1 / rockchip,rga2_core0 rather
than from probe order. The register window grows to the full 4 KiB each
core occupies, because the driver programs the core's IOMMU through that
window at offset 0xf00; the 0x200 and 0x180 windows stop short of it.

The separate rga3_0_mmu / rga3_1_mmu nodes stay as they are, bound by
rockchip-iommu as before, and no clock, reset, interrupt or power-domain
property moves: the driver takes its clocks with clk_bulk_get_all and
looks up no reset or interrupt by name.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
index 56045969abee..597317167b8e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-base.dtsi
@@ -1265,8 +1265,8 @@ vpu121_mmu: iommu@fdb50800 {
 	};
 
 	rga3_core0: rga@fdb60000 {
-		compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-rga3";
-		reg = <0x0 0xfdb60000 0x0 0x200>;
+		compatible = "rockchip,rga3_core0";
+		reg = <0x0 0xfdb60000 0x0 0x1000>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 114 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 		clocks = <&cru ACLK_RGA3_0>, <&cru HCLK_RGA3_0>, <&cru CLK_RGA3_0_CORE>;
 		clock-names = "aclk", "hclk", "sclk";
@@ -1287,8 +1287,8 @@ rga3_0_mmu: iommu@fdb60f00 {
 	};
 
 	rga3_core1: rga@fdb70000 {
-		compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-rga3";
-		reg = <0x0 0xfdb70000 0x0 0x200>;
+		compatible = "rockchip,rga3_core1";
+		reg = <0x0 0xfdb70000 0x0 0x1000>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 115 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 		clocks = <&cru ACLK_RGA3_1>, <&cru HCLK_RGA3_1>, <&cru CLK_RGA3_1_CORE>;
 		clock-names = "aclk", "hclk", "sclk";
@@ -1308,9 +1308,9 @@ rga3_1_mmu: iommu@fdb70f00 {
 		power-domains = <&power RK3588_PD_RGA31>;
 	};
 
-	rga: rga@fdb80000 {
-		compatible = "rockchip,rk3588-rga", "rockchip,rk3288-rga";
-		reg = <0x0 0xfdb80000 0x0 0x180>;
+	rga2: rga@fdb80000 {
+		compatible = "rockchip,rga2_core0";
+		reg = <0x0 0xfdb80000 0x0 0x1000>;
 		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 116 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH 0>;
 		clocks = <&cru ACLK_RGA2>, <&cru HCLK_RGA2>, <&cru CLK_RGA2_CORE>;
 		clock-names = "aclk", "hclk", "sclk";
-- 
